## Obligations when you redistribute a binary

The MIT and Apache-2.0 licences both require you to carry their notices with any
binary you distribute. If you build and ship `nova-compiler`, `nova-lsp`,
`nova-pkg` or `nova-dbg`, you must reproduce the copyright notice and permission
notice for every dependency in the tree, not just the ones in the table above.

Generate that bundle rather than assembling it by hand:

```bash
cargo install cargo-about
cargo about generate about.hbs > THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.html
```

The Windows binary in `dist/` is a prebuilt artifact of this project. It is
distributed under the same MIT licence as the source, with the third-party
notices above applying to it in the same way.

